 "NASA-STD-# Vol. #, Table #": "NASA-STD-# Vol. #, Tabla #",
 "NASA: a Mars mission takes “roughly three years”. Beyond # months the line is the app's extrapolation.": "NASA: una misión a Marte dura “roughly three years”. Más allá de # meses, la línea es una extrapolación de la app.",
 "NASA: no more than # mmHg (#-hour average)": "NASA: no más de # mmHg (promedio de # h)",
 "NASA's clip-on CO₂ monitor: “The Personal CO# Monitor was then paired to the iPad”. “The data collected will be uploaded to the Space Station Computer via the iPad app before being powered off and stowed.”": "Monitor de CO₂ de clip de NASA: “The Personal CO# Monitor was then paired to the iPad”. “The data collected will be uploaded to the Space Station Computer via the iPad app before being powered off and stowed.”",
 "NASA's CO₂ limit is a #-hour average. The simulator compares the current value so the demo reacts in seconds; a real detector would average over the hour. Crew vital signs are judged on a #-second average so one noisy reading raises nothing. An alert is raised after # readings in a row and cleared after # back to normal.": "El límite de CO₂ de NASA es un promedio de # h. El simulador compara el valor actual para que la demostración reaccione en segundos; un detector real promediaría durante la hora. Los signos vitales de la tripulación se evalúan con un promedio de # segundos, así que una sola lectura con ruido no activa nada. Una alerta se activa tras # lecturas seguidas y se borra tras # de vuelta a lo normal.",
